# The network of "Follow the route": three sites, each behind a router of
# its own, and the three routers joined in a triangle.
#
#   office 10.1.0.10 --- r1 ---------- r2 --- store 10.2.0.10
#                          \          /
#                           \        /
#                               r3 --- dc 10.3.0.10 (a web server)
#
# Each router's interfaces are named after what is at the far end of the
# cable: on r1, "r2" goes to r2, "r3" to r3 and "lan" to the office. The
# hosts have a default route to their own router; the routers start with
# no routes beyond their own networks, and their routes belong in FRR.
machine office
machine store
machine dc
machine r1 router
machine r2 router
machine r3 router

link office:eth0=10.1.0.10/24 r1:lan=10.1.0.1/24
link store:eth0=10.2.0.10/24 r2:lan=10.2.0.1/24
link dc:eth0=10.3.0.10/24 r3:lan=10.3.0.1/24
link r1:r2=10.0.12.1/30 r2:r1=10.0.12.2/30
link r1:r3=10.0.13.1/30 r3:r1=10.0.13.2/30
link r2:r3=10.0.23.1/30 r3:r2=10.0.23.2/30

route office default via 10.1.0.1
route store default via 10.2.0.1
route dc default via 10.3.0.1

run r1 frr
run r2 frr
run r3 frr
run dc nginx
